.TH RNDIR 1.SH NAMErndir \- change the case of directory names.SH SYNOPSIS\fBrndir\fR[\-dlnq] [\-h].SH DESCRIPTION\fBrndir\fRscans the tree under the current directory and renames the directoriesin capitals, or with\fB\-l\fRin small letters -- its own description is "rename directory names inbig/small characters".  It works through temporary files, written to theroot of the device unless\fB\-d\fRputs them in the current directory.  By F. R. Schmitt, 1990..PPUnder os9exec it scans and renames nothing, with or without a RAM diskfor its temporary files; what it is waiting for has not beenestablished.\fBupperdir\fRdoes the same job on one directory and works..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-l\fRsmall letters..TP 12\fB\-d\fRtemporary files in the current directory..TP 12\fB\-n\fRkeep the temporary files afterwards..TP 12\fB\-q\fRquiet..TP 12\fB\-h\fRhelp..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOupperdir